rows.en:
I was tense as I counted, carefully, one step at a time, so I wouldn't make a mistake.
"Ten... eleven... twelve... thirteen..................fourteen."
Fourteen steps, again.{p}

Something else...?
Yeah, it's wrong to decide that everything suspicious is a ghost.
It could be an alien, or it could be a yokai.{p}

Thanks.
You can't know for sure unless you check both ways, after all.
We checked the number of steps going down, too.{p}

Ah...!
{c}{f:|}☆
At your feet, {c}{f:|}... there's a baby...{p}

{c}{f:|}, you said earlier that you'd been to the old school building, right?
Didn't you go by that staircase?
That staircase should still have a tear-off calendar on its wall even now.{p}

Ah... it vanished.
But you saw it, didn't you?
You saw it, right?{p}

{f:That's right|That's right}.
The wooden floorboards had definitely been creaking.
And then the end of the hallway drew closer..........{p}

Ishikawa slipped the ring onto the ring finger of her left hand right away.
On Ishikawa's left hand, the ring gave off an even more sinister glow.
And then...{p}
